// The BRACED selective import with an alias — `lib.{config as cfg, spare}` —
// which is the spelling `nomi fmt` keeps once the list has more than one item,
// and the one the corpus's explicit_item_imports_test.nomi uses.
//
// `cfg` is the case that matters: it is bound locally while the declaration is
// `config`, and decoy.nomi declares its own `pub once config` and sorts BEFORE
// lib.nomi. So a resolution that read the local spelling MISSES, and one that
// searched units by the declared name answers 99 where 7 is correct.
import {
    std/io
    decoy
    lib.{config as cfg, spare}
}

fn main() {
    io.print("${cfg}")
    io.print("${spare}")
    io.print("${decoy.reveal()}")
}
